SUMMARY:Clark Nature Preserve Field Trip
DESCRIPTION:Sarah Gotwols will lead a walk through the Clark Nature Preserve to explore the meadow and woodlands for summer birds such as buntings\, vireo\, and tanagers. Meet in the parking area at the end of House Rock Road at 7 a.m. There will be a moderate intensity walk along the Ralph H. Goodno Trail and “Blue Trail” which leads to Reed Run and the House Rock overlook as well as the newly-opened universally accessible trail. Please bring water and snacks\, binoculars\, and be prepared for insects including ticks. Contact Sarah (717-940-3804 call/text or email sarahann71880@gmail.com) by 6 p.m. on Friday if you plan to attend. If necessary\, weather-related cancelations will be made the day prior and registered participants will be notified. \n\nLocation: Clark Nature Preserve\, 400 House Rock Road\, Pequea\, PA \nContact: Sarah Gotwols (717) 940-3804 or sarahann71880@gmail.com
URL:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/event/clark-nature-preserve-field-trip/
LOCATION:Clark Nature Preserve\, 400 House Rock Rd\, Pequea\, PA\, 17565\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://lancasterbirdclub.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/IMG_8547.jpeg
